{"type":"message","id":"64eeccfe","parentId":"c2b9a0ba","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:42:15.363Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user asked to \"Stop running heart beats\".\nPreviously I checked cron jobs, but none of the cron jobs were named heartbeat.\nThen I remembered that heartbeats are configured in `agents.defaults.heartbeat`.\nI ran `openclaw config get agents.defaults.heartbeat` and saw:\n```json\n{\n  \"every\": \"30m\"\n}\n```\nI then ran `openclaw config unset agents.defaults.heartbeat`.\nIt said `Removed agents.defaults.heartbeat. Restart the gateway to apply.`\nI tried to restart the gateway via `openclaw gateway restart`, but it failed.\nThen I tried `systemctl --user restart openclaw-gateway`, but it aborted due to timeout? Wait, it was `systemctl --user status openclaw-gateway` which showed that the service *did* restart recently (\"Active: active (running) since Thu 2026-05-21 12:41:00 UTC; 42s ago\"). The process pid changed, so the restart actually succeeded despite the SIGTERM warning for the `restart` command itself.\n\nLet me verify that the heartbeat is actually gone from config and the system."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"kpk0xx5s","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw config get agents.defaults.heartbeat"},"thoughtSignature":"EiYKJGUyNDgzMGE3LTVjZDYtNDJmZS05OThiLWVlNTM5ZTcyYjljMw=="},{"type":"text","text":""}],"api":"google-generative-ai","provider":"google","model":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","usage":{"input":3305,"output":288,"cacheRead":24657,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28250,"cost":{"input":0.0066099999999999996,"output":0.003456,"cacheRead":0.004931400000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0149974}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779367328374,"responseId":"oP0Oar22Js6WvdIP5JPBkQo"}}
